{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1396331-mixed-questions","id":1396331,"title":"Mixed questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-14T01:35:02-07:00","id":1396331,"title":"Mixed questions","content":"I got all sorts of questions <br /> <br /> 1st<br /> Casting a spell. Its gnosis + acanum + bonus(what ever that may be). If i want to instand cast i can only use one bonus (yantra) no matter what. Thats the basic spell casting as i understand it.<br /> <br /> <br /> 2nd <br /> how do you handel time, when traveling rounds back in time or a scene. Do you delete the other players actions and give them all lost damage back and mana ect..<br /> <br /> 3ed <br /> in 1ed as spirit 5 you could create a spirit court, can this be done at spirit 5 in 2nd<br /> <br /> 4ed<br /> for creating or summening golems..ghosts..zombies..bee-zombiees.....ect, is reach asways used for determining rank.<br /> <br /> 5ed<br /> is paime factor Duration or potency is always arcanum -1 for free. For a base spell.<br /> <br /> 6ed<br /> what are you general thoughts regarding the special rules compared to first edition what\u2019s the pros and cons.<br /> <br /> thanks<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6707-exkramental","name":"Exkramental","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T03:39:07-07:00","id":1396342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exkramental</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1396331-mixed-questions#post1396331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got all sorts of questions <br /> <br /> 1st<br /> Casting a spell. Its gnosis + acanum + bonus(what ever that may be). If i want to instand cast i can only use one bonus (yantra) no matter what. Thats the basic spell casting as i understand it.<br /> <br /> <br /> 2nd <br /> how do you handel time, when traveling rounds back in time or a scene. Do you delete the other players actions and give them all lost damage back and mana ect..<br /> <br /> 3ed <br /> in 1ed as spirit 5 you could create a spirit court, can this be done at spirit 5 in 2nd<br /> <br /> 4ed<br /> for creating or summening golems..ghosts..zombies..bee-zombiees.....ect, is reach asways used for determining rank.<br /> <br /> 5ed<br /> is paime factor Duration or potency is always arcanum -1 for free. For a base spell.<br /> <br /> 6ed<br /> what are you general thoughts regarding the special rules compared to first edition what\u2019s the pros and cons.<br /> <br /> thanks<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>1st, you can use a yantra per turn, up to your gnosis derived maximum","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T04:47:40-07:00","id":1396352,"title":"","content":"1.) Not phrased as a question, but no. You can use multiple Yantras for an instant spell. Each Yantra after the first will just require additional instant actions. The spell you cast will still be cast as an instant action the turn after you added the last Yantra.<br /> <br /> 3.) Probably.<br /> <br /> 4.) Only if whatever you create uses Rank. Generally, only ephemeral entities (and Supernal entities; but you can't <i>create</i> them) have Rank so it's not applicable on golems or zombies. You could create golems and zombies by having ephemeral entities possess the physical bodies, but then Rank is determined by whatever Rank the entity had; not the amount of Reach you've spent.<br /> <br /> 5.) All spell factors start at 1. You <i>add</i> [Arcanum dots - 1] to the primary spell factor. In practice this means that the primary spell factor starts at [Arcanum dots].","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T05:36:38-07:00","id":1396362,"title":"","content":"3. You don't even need to use a spell. You get a Spirit Rank equivalent to your ability in the Spirit Arcanum as an Attainment when you reach Spirit 4, this lets you become respected among Spirits. The lore mentions that generally Spirits of at least Rank 5 tend to lead their own Courts, so you will likely want Spirit 5 to have Rank 5 as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T06:55:48-07:00","id":1396368,"title":"","content":"6ed<br /> The emphasis on yantras makes spellcasting more engaging from a RP and flavor perspective, and helps players involved think more about mystic symbolism as it applies to their characters. It works well if the players and ST take the time to give yantras the attention they deserve. Otherwise they just turn into hoops you jump through for bonuses.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}